H4700.definition:
from H6750 (צָלַל);
(only dual) double tinklers, i.e. cymbals
KJV: cymbals.

H4701.definition:
from H6801 (צָנַף);
a tiara, i.e. official turban (of a king or high priest)
KJV: diadem, mitre.

H4702.definition:
from H3331 (יַצַע);
a couch
KJV: bed.

H4703.definition:
from H6805 (צָעַד);
a step; figuratively, companionship
KJV: going, step.

H4704.definition:
feminine of H4705 (מִצְעָר);
properly, littleness; concretely, diminutive
KJV: little.

H4705.definition:
from H6819 (צָעַר);
petty (in size or number); adverbially, a short (time)
KJV: little one (while), small.

H4706.definition:
the same as H4705 (מִצְעָר);
Mitsar, a peak of Lebanon
KJV: Mizar.

H4707.definition:
from H6822 (צָפָה);
an observatory, especially formilitary purposes
KJV: watch tower.

H4708.definition:
the same as H4707 (מִצְפֶּה);
Mitspeh, the name of five places in Palestine
KJV: Mizpeh, watch tower. Compare H4709 (מִצְפָּה).

H4709.definition:
feminine of H4708 (מִצְפֶּה);
Mitspah, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Mitspah. (This seems rather to be only an orthographic variation of H4708 (מִצְפֶּה) when 'in pause'.)

H4710.definition:
from H6845 (צָפַן);
a secret (place or thing, perhaps, treasure)
KJV: hidden thing.

H4711.definition:
a primitive root;
to suck
KJV: milk.

H4712.definition:
from H6896 (קֵבָה);
something tight, i.e. (figuratively) trouble
KJV: distress, pain, strait.

H4713.definition:
from H4714 (מִצְרַיִם);
a Mitsrite, or inhabitant of Mitsrajim
KJV: Egyptian, of Egypt.

H4714.definition:
dual of H4693 (מָצוֹר);
Mitsrajim, i.e. Upper and Lower Egypt
KJV: Egypt, Egyptians, Mizraim.

H4715.definition:
from H6884 (צָרַף);
a crucible
KJV: fining pot.

H4716.definition:
from H4743 (מָקַק);
properly, a melting, i.e. putridity
KJV: rottenness, stink.

H4717.definition:
from H5344 (נָקַב);
properly, a perforatrix, i.e. a hammer (as piercing)
KJV: hammer.

H4718.definition:
from H5344 (נָקַב);
properly, a perforator, i.e. a hammer (as piercing); also (intransitively) a perforation, i.e. a quarry
KJV: hammer, hole.

H4719.definition:
from the same as H5348 (נָקֹד) in the denominative sense of herding (compare H5349 (נֹקֵד)); fold;
Makkedah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Makkedah.

H4720.definition:
or מִקְּדָשׁ; (Exodus 15:17), from H6942 (קָדַשׁ);
a consecrated thing or place, especially, a palace, sanctuary (whether of Jehovah or of idols) or asylum
KJV: chapel, hallowed part, holy place, sanctuary.

H4721.definition:
or (feminine) מַקְהֵלָה; from H6950 (קָהַל);
an assembly
KJV: congregation.

H4722.definition:
plural of H4721 (מַקְהֵל) (feminine); assemblies;
Makheloth, a place in the Desert
KJV: Makheloth.

H4723.definition:
or מִקְוֵה; (1 Kings 10:28), or מִקְוֵאlemma מִּקְוֵא extra dagesh, corrected to מִקְוֵא; (2 Chronicles 1:16), from H6960 (קָוָה);
something waited for, i.e. confidence (objective or subjective); also a collection, i.e. (of water) a pond, or (of men and horses) a caravan or drove
KJV: abiding, gathering together, hope, linen yarn, plenty (of water), pool.

H4724.definition:
feminine of H4723 (מִקְוֶה);
a collection, i.e. (of water) a reservoir
KJV: ditch.

H4725.definition:
or מָקֹם; also (feminine) מְקוֹמָה; or מְקֹמָה; from H6965 (קוּם);
properly, a standing, i.e. a spot; but used widely of a locality (general or specific); also (figuratively) of a condition (of body or mind)
KJV: country, [idiom] home, [idiom] open, place, room, space, [idiom] whither(-soever).

H4726.definition:
or מָקֹר; from H6979 (קוּר);
properly, something dug, i.e. a (general) source (of water, even when naturally flowing; also of tears, blood (by euphemism, of the female pudenda); figuratively, of happiness, wisdom, progeny)
KJV: fountain, issue, spring, well(-spring).

H4728.definition:
from H3947 (לָקַח);
something received, i.e. merchandise (purchased)
KJV: ware.

H4729.definition:
from H6999 (קָטַר);
something to fume (incense) on i.e. a hearth place
KJV: to burn...upon.

H4730.definition:
feminine of H4729 (מִקְטָר);
something to fume (incense) in, i.e. a coal-pan
KJV: censer.

H4731.definition:
or (feminine) מַקְּלָה; from an unused root meaning apparently to germinate;
a shoot, i.e. stick (with leaves on, or for walking, striking, guiding, divining)
KJV: rod, (hand-)staff.

H4732.definition:
(or perhaps mik-kel-ohth') plural of (feminine) H4731 (מַקֵּל); rods;
Mikloth, a place in the Desert
KJV: Mikloth.

H4733.definition:
from H7038 (קָלַט) in the sense of taking in;
an asylum (as a receptacle)
KJV: refuge.

H4734.definition:
from H7049 (קָלַע);
a sculpture (probably in bas-relief)
KJV: carved (figure), carving, graving.

H4735.definition:
from H7069 (קָנָה);
something bought, i.e. property, but only livestock; abstractly, acquisition
KJV: cattle, flock, herd, possession, purchase, substance.

H4736.definition:
feminine of H4735 (מִקְנֶה);
properly, a buying, i.e. acquisition; concretely, a piece of property (land or living); also the sum paid
KJV: (he that is) bought, possession, piece, purchase.

H4737.definition:
from H4735 (מִקְנֶה) and H3050 (יָהּ); possession of Jah;
Miknejah, an Israelite
KJV: Mikneiah.

H4738.definition:
from H7080 (קָסַם);
an augury
KJV: divination.

H4739.definition:
from H7112 (קָצַץ); end;
Makats, a place in Palestine
KJV: Makaz.

H4740.definition:
or מַקְצֹעַ; or (feminine) מַקְצֹעָה; from H7106 (קָצַע) in the denominative sense of bending;
an angle or recess
KJV: corner, turning.

H4741.definition:
from H7106 (קָצַע);
a scraper, i.e. a carving chisel
KJV: plane.

H4742.definition:
from H7106 (קָצַע) in the denominative sense of bending;
an angle
KJV: corner.

H4743.definition:
' a primitive root;
to melt; figuratively, to flow, dwindle, vanish
KJV: consume away, be corrupt, dissolve, pine away.

H4744.definition:
from H7121 (קָרָא);
something called out, i.e. a public meeting (the act, the persons, or the place); also a rehearsal
KJV: assembly, calling, convocation, reading.

H4745.definition:
from H7136 (קָרָה);
something met with, i.e. an accident or fortune
KJV: something befallen, befalleth, chance, event, hap(-peneth).

H4746.definition:
from H7136 (קָרָה);
properly, something meeting, i.e. a frame (of timbers)
KJV: building.

H4747.definition:
from the same as H7119 (קַר);
a cooling off
KJV: [idiom] summer.

H4748.definition:
from H7185 (קָשָׁה) in the sense of knotting up round and hard;
something turned (rounded), i.e. a curl (of tresses)
KJV: [idiom] well (set) hair.

H4749.definition:
feminine of H4748 (מִקְשֶׁה);
rounded work, i.e. moulded by hammering (repousse)
KJV: beaten (out of one piece, work), upright, whole piece.

H4750.definition:
denominative from H7180 (קִשֻּׁא);
literally a cucumbered field, i.e. a cucumber patch
KJV: garden of cucumbers.

H4751.definition:
or (feminine) מָרָה; from H4843 (מָרַר);
bitter (literally or figuratively); also (as noun) bitterness, or (adverbially) bitterly
KJV: [phrase] angry, bitter(-ly, -ness), chafed, discontented, [idiom] great, heavy.

H4752.definition:
from H4843 (מָרַר) in its original sense of distillation;
a drop
KJV: drop.

H4753.definition:
or מוֹר; from H4843 (מָרַר);
myrrh (as distilling in drops, and also as bitter)
KJV: myrrh.

H4754.definition:
a primitive root;
to rebel; hence (through the idea of maltreating) to whip, i.e. lash (self with wings, as the ostrich in running)
KJV: be filthy, lift up self.

H4755.definition:
for H4751 (מַר) feminine; bitter;
Mara, a symbolic name of Naomi
KJV: Mara.

H4756.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H4754 (מָרָא) in the sense of domineering;
a master
KJV: lord, Lord.

H4757.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Merodak-Baladan, a Babylonian king
KJV: Merodach-baladan. Compare H4781 (מְרֹדָךְ).

H4758.definition:
from H7200 (רָאָה);
a view (the act of seeing); also an appearance (the thing seen), whether (real) a shape (especially if handsome, comeliness; often plural the looks), or (mental) a vision
KJV: [idiom] apparently, appearance(-reth), [idiom] as soon as beautiful(-ly), countenance, fair, favoured, form, goodly, to look (up) on (to), look(-eth), pattern, to see, seem, sight, visage, vision.

H4759.definition:
feminine of H4758 (מַרְאֶה);
a vision; also (causatively) a mirror
KJV: looking glass, vision.

H4760.definition:
apparently feminine passive causative participle of H7200 (רָאָה);
something conspicuous, i.e. the craw of abird (from its prominence)
KJV: crop.

H4761.definition:
denominative from H7218 (רֹאשׁ);
properly, headship, i.e. (plural for collective) dominion
KJV: principality.

H4762.definition:
or מַרֵשָׁה; formed like H4761 (מַרְאָשָׁה); summit;
Mareshah, the name of two Israelites and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Mareshah.

H4763.definition:
formed like H4761 (מַרְאָשָׁה);
properly, a headpiece, i.e. (plural for adverbial) at (or as) the head-rest (or pillow)
KJV: bolster, head, pillow. Compare H4772 (מַרְגְלָה).

H4764.definition:
from H7231 (רָבַב); increase;
Merab, a daughter of Saul
KJV: Merab.

H4765.definition:
from H7234 (רָבַד);
a coverlet
KJV: covering of tapestry.

H4766.definition:
from H7235 (רָבָה);
properly, increasing; as noun, greatness, or (adverbially) greatly
KJV: great, increase.

H4767.definition:
from H7235 (רָבָה);
abundance, i.e. a great quantity
KJV: much.

H4768.definition:
from H7235 (רָבָה);
a multitude; also offspring; specifically interest (on capital)
KJV: greatest part, greatness, increase, multitude.

H4769.definition:
from H7257 (רָבַץ);
a reclining place, i.e. fold (for flocks)
KJV: couching place, place to lie down.

H4770.definition:
from an unused root meaning to tie up;
a stall (for cattle)
KJV: [idiom] fat(-ted), stall.

H4771.definition:
from H7280 (רָגַע);
a resting place
KJV: rest.

H4772.definition:
denominative from H7272 (רֶגֶל);
(plural for collective) a footpiece, i.e. (adverbially) at the foot, or (direct.) the foot itself
KJV: feet. Compare H4763 (מְרַאֲשָׁה).

H4773.definition:
from H7275 (רָגַם);
a stone-heap
KJV: sling.

H4775.definition:
a primitive root;
to rebel
KJV: rebel(-lious).

H4776.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H4775 (מָרַד);
rebellion
KJV: rebellion.

H4778.definition:
the same as H4777 (מֶרֶד);
Mered, an Israelite
KJV: Mered.

H4779.definition:
(Aramaic) from the same as H4776 (מְרַד);
rebellious
KJV: rebellious.

H4781.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Merodak, a Babylonian idol
KJV: Merodach. Compare H4757 (מְרֹאדַךְ בַּלְאָדָן).

H4782.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Mordecai, an Israelite
KJV: Mordecai.

H4784.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, make) bitter (or unpleasant); (figuratively) to rebel (or resist; causatively, to provoke)
KJV: bitter, change, be disobedient, disobey, grievously, provocation, provoke(-ing), (be) rebel (against, -lious).

H4785.definition:
the same as H4751 (מַר) feminine; bitter;
Marah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Marah.

H4786.definition:
from H4843 (מָרַר);
bitterness, i.e. (figuratively) trouble
KJV: grief.

H4787.definition:
a form of H4786 (מֹרָה);
trouble
KJV: bitterness.

H4788.definition:
from H7300 (רוּד) in the sense of maltreatment;
an outcast; (abstractly) destitution
KJV: cast out, misery.

H4789.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Meroz, a place in Palestine
KJV: Meroz.

H4790.definition:
from H4799 (מָרַח);
bruised, i.e. emasculated
KJV: broken.

H4791.definition:
from H7311 (רוּם);
altitude, i.e. concretely (an elevated place), abstractly (elevation, figuratively (elation), or adverbially (aloft)
KJV: (far) above, dignity, haughty, height, (most, on) high (one, place), loftily, upward.

H4792.definition:
formed like H4791 (מָרוֹם); height;
Merom, a lake in Palestine
KJV: Merom.

H4793.definition:
from H7323 (רוּץ);
a run (the trial of speed)
KJV: race.

H4794.definition:
or מְרֻצָה; feminine of H4793 (מֵרוֹץ);
a race (the act), whether the manner or the progress
KJV: course, running. Compare H4835 (מְרֻצָה).

H4795.definition:
from H4838 (מָרַק);
properly, rubbed; but used abstractly, a rubbing (with perfumery)
KJV: purification.

H4796.definition:
plural of H4751 (מַר) feminine; bitter springs;
Maroth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Maroth.

H4797.definition:
from an unused root meaning to scream;
a cry, i.e. (of job), a revel
KJV: banquet.

H4798.definition:
formed like H4797 (מִרְזַח);
a cry, i.e. (of grief) a lamentation
KJV: mourning.

H4799.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to soften by rubbing or pressure; hence (medicinally) to apply as an emollient
KJV: lay for a plaister.
